/E (Learning Management Systems \(LMS\) have revolutionized the way operators train their staff, providing a structured and efficient alternative to traditional training methods. With features that allow for the creation of customized training materials, testing and scoring capabilities, and the automatic assignment of learning modules, LMS platforms not only streamline the training process but also allow operators to track staff progress in real-time. This enhanced visibility into employee development is crucial for ensuring that team members acquire the essential skills and knowledge necessary for success. However, the financial commitment required for these systems can be a significant hurdle, with costs ranging from $400 to $3,000 per month for a restaurant employing around 50 staff. Given the multitude of technology solutions that operators must integrate to maintain competitiveness, investing in comprehensive training often falls by the wayside.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
278 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 204 0 R
/E (The consequences of inadequate training can be detrimental, with many establishments rely on the informal transfer of knowledge from one employee to another, which may not always be comprehensive or accurate. This reliance can result in poorly trained employees who lack the essential information and skills required for their roles, ultimately impacting the overall performance of the restaurant. Acknowledging this challenge, we have integrated an LMS into our app, providing staff with easy access to training materials, handbooks, and assessments. As employees engage with this content, they receive scores reflecting their understanding and retention of the material relevant to their position. Managers can effortlessly track the progress of each team member within the same app they use to monitor key performance indicators \(KPIs\), ensuring that training and operational efficiency go hand-in-hand.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
