/P 221 0 R
/E (As new entrepreneurs, it's easy to see our inexperience as a high-risk factor, and the practical challenges we face while running a business for the first time can indeed lead to common pitfalls. Issues like cash flow mismanagement, lack of focus, and poor delegation can derail even the most promising ventures. The immense pressure to succeed often translates into long hours and an unhealthy work-life balance, which can culminate in burnout. However, these weaknesses are not permanent; they can be addressed and transformed. By cultivating a strong, experienced team, investing in our own skill development, and consciously tackling these pitfalls rather than avoiding them, we can pave the way for sustainable growth and success in our entrepreneurial journeys. )
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
