/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 222 0 R
/T (HIGHER CUSTOMER ACQUISTION COSTS  High customer acquisition costs \(CAC\) for restaurant technology are often a result of long sales cycles, skepticism about ROI, and fierce competition for limited budgets. Given their typically thin profit margins, restaurant operators are understandably cautious about adopting new tools, fearing potential disruptions to established workflows, technical glitches during peak hours, and the steep learning curves associated with new technology. This hesitation necessitates a trust-building process that goes beyond simple digital marketing, often requiring a consultative, in-person approach that can drive up personnel costs. Many operators struggle to visualize how a new technology might enhance profitability or enrich the guest experience, which is reflected in their tendency to allocate a minimal percentage of annual revenue to technological investments. As a tech company with deep roots in the restaurant industry, we truly understand the operators' perspective and the importance of their bottom line. Having experienced numerous pitches ourselves, we know the most effective ways to engage with restaurant owners - after all, we want to be approached in ways that resonate with us. Our focus on one-on-one, in-person interactions allows us to foster genuine connections with clients, and by utilizing our own technology within our restaurant, we can directly demonstrate to owners how our app enhances both profitability and operational efficiency.)
/E (HIGHER CUSTOMER ACQUISTION COSTS  High customer acquisition costs \(CAC\) for restaurant technology are often a result of long sales cycles, skepticism about ROI, and fierce competition for limited budgets. Given their typically thin profit margins, restaurant operators are understandably cautious about adopting new tools, fearing potential disruptions to established workflows, technical glitches during peak hours, and the steep learning curves associated with new technology. This hesitation necessitates a trust-building process that goes beyond simple digital marketing, often requiring a consultative, in-person approach that can drive up personnel costs. Many operators struggle to visualize how a new technology might enhance profitability or enrich the guest experience, which is reflected in their tendency to allocate a minimal percentage of annual revenue to technological investments. As a tech company with deep roots in the restaurant industry, we truly understand the operators' perspective and the importance of their bottom line. Having experienced numerous pitches ourselves, we know the most effective ways to engage with restaurant owners - after all, we want to be approached in ways that resonate with us. Our focus on one-on-one, in-person interactions allows us to foster genuine connections with clients, and by utilizing our own technology within our restaurant, we can directly demonstrate to owners how our app enhances both profitability and operational efficiency.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
