/E (In today's rapidly evolving tech landscape, platform dependency poses a significant risk to applications through potential single points of failure, particularly when relying on major third-party providers like AWS, Apple, or Google. This reliance can lead to catastrophic consequences, including unexpected downtime, abrupt policy shifts, or algorithm changes that can wipe out visibility and revenue in an instant. To mitigate these risks, we are proactively diversifying our infrastructure by avoiding exclusive reliance on a single cloud provider or API. By adopting cross-platform development frameworks, we minimize our dependence on native iOS and Android tools, ensuring our applications remain flexible and adaptable. Furthermore, we design our systems to be easily migratable to new providers by decoupling backend services and  continuous monitor the health, security, and updates of external APIs. )
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
