/P 226 0 R
/T (CYBERSECURITY ATTACKS  Cybersecurity attacks are increasingly targeting startups and restaurants, often perceived as vulnerable due to their limited resources and security practices. Startups, often brimming with valuable intellectual property and innovative solutions, face risks from attackers looking to exploit weak defenses in pursuit of sensitive data or as gateways to larger partners through supply chain attacks. Meanwhile, restaurants, rich in guest information yet often lacking robust IT investments, present an appealing target for cybercriminals, especially given their reliance on third-party platforms which expands the attack surface, outdated POS systems using weak encryption, and connection to unsecure networks. The potential for reputation-damaging breaches looms large, which is why we have prioritized rigorous third-party security audits to safeguard against these threats. By enhancing our security posture, we protect our assets allowing us to build trust and confidence among our clients.)
/E (CYBERSECURITY ATTACKS  Cybersecurity attacks are increasingly targeting startups and restaurants, often perceived as vulnerable due to their limited resources and security practices. Startups, often brimming with valuable intellectual property and innovative solutions, face risks from attackers looking to exploit weak defenses in pursuit of sensitive data or as gateways to larger partners through supply chain attacks. Meanwhile, restaurants, rich in guest information yet often lacking robust IT investments, present an appealing target for cybercriminals, especially given their reliance on third-party platforms which expands the attack surface, outdated POS systems using weak encryption, and connection to unsecure networks. The potential for reputation-damaging breaches looms large, which is why we have prioritized rigorous third-party security audits to safeguard against these threats. By enhancing our security posture, we protect our assets allowing us to build trust and confidence among our clients.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
