/P 228 0 R
/E (In the quest to enhance convenience for guests, many emerging trends have introduced solutions such as QR code ordering at tables, interactive tabletops, and chatbots for reservations. While these advancements certainly help alleviate some labor shortages, they can inadvertently detract from the essential human interaction that defines a memorable dining experience. The reality is that labor shortages often stem from deeper-rooted issues, such as a lack of positive company culture. Our focus is on empowering management to engage directly with guests instead of being bogged down by administrative tasks. By freeing staff from these duties, we enable them to focus on the guest-facing elements that truly matter. Automated systems may offer convenience, but the absence of personalized interactions leaves guests longing for the guidance that enhances their dining experience - such as in-depth menu explanations and personalized recommendations.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [1]
>>
